Chapter: EffectLaunderRecord
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Adversarial probe (effect rows stage 0). Data-structure
 laundering: an effectful function stored into a record field whose
 declared type is a pure arrow, then called through the field from
 a def declared pure. Field unification strips the effect under
 flat effects. Effect rows stage 3b rejects the construction: the
 declared pure field row is closed and cannot reconcile with the
 stored closure's opened Console row (CDX2090). This test is the
 enforcement's regression guard.

Section: Definitions

  boom : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  boom (n) = act
    print-line-uni "field boom"
    n
  end

  Holder = record {
   fn : Integer -> Integer
  }

  quiet : Integer -> Integer
  quiet (n) =
   let h = Holder { fn = boom }
   in (h.fn) n

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("result " & show (quiet 41))
  end
